Third-party dependency evidence

Tevari's own terms are in LICENSE. Third-party components remain subject to
their separate licences; LICENSE does not override those terms.

This source export declares dependencies in pyproject.toml and preserves the
native build tooling and hash-locked dependency inputs. Native builds generate
dependency-licences.json, sbom.cyclonedx.json and sbom.spdx.json alongside the
release artifacts using the resolved build environment. These generated files
are dependency evidence, not an approval of licence compatibility or a substitute
for applicable upstream notices and licence texts.

For each release, retain the resolved dependency versions and applicable upstream
licence and notice files from the built artifacts separately from Tevari's LICENSE.
The source export does not vendor dependency wheels or their licence texts.

Gitleaks scanner rule configuration

requirements/secret-scanning.toml derives from Gitleaks v8.30.1:
https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/tree/v8.30.1
Upstream rules and value allowlists are retained. Global path exclusions are
limited to Git metadata; a credential-bearing Authorization header rule is added.
